.TH BRAIN 1 "" "brain 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
brain \- agent\-native semantic substrate: one graph for code, twin, decisions, tests, and docs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B brain
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
brain keeps software knowledge in a content\-addressed graph: what the software is (files, symbols, imports), why it is that way (decisions, plans), how it is built (skills, agent configuration), what done means (templates, a definition of done), what happened (test protocols, timelines), and what matters now (attention). Facts are immutable, sourced, timestamped observations \- history is the data model, not a feature. Git hooks keep the graph fresh on every commit; replication moves truth between stores as a set union.
.SH STORE
The system of record: a content\-addressed graph in .brain/ \(em immutable objects, an append\-only event log, namespace lineage as version control.
.TP
.B brain init
create a store in ./.brain and seed the deliverable templates
.TP
.B brain status
objects, namespace size, HEAD, intent states
.TP
.B brain names
list name \-> node bindings
.TP
.B brain pull \fI<store\-root>\fR
replicate another store into this one (set union, conflicts preserved)
.TP
.B brain push \fI<store\-root>\fR
replicate this store into another
.SH TWIN
Reflective mode: a persistent, queryable semantic model of existing software. Observations are sourced and timestamped; only drift is recorded.
.TP
.B brain twin refresh \fI<dir> [\-\-prefix <p>] [\-\-full]\fR
observe a source tree, record only drift; \-\-full reprocesses every file after extractor upgrades
.TP
.B brain twin status \fI<dir> [\-\-prefix <p>]\fR
the same comparison, read\-only
.TP
.B brain twin backfill \fI<dir> [\-\-prefix <p>] [\-\-max\-commits N]\fR
replay git history into the twin with historical timestamps (brownfield minute\-one)
.TP
.B brain twin files \fI<prefix>\fR
twinned files with language, symbols, freshness
.TP
.B brain twin symbols \fI<name>\fR
what a file declares, with line numbers
.TP
.B brain twin imports \fI<name> [\-\-transitive]\fR
what a file depends on; \-\-transitive walks the closure
.TP
.B brain twin rdeps \fI<name> [\-\-transitive]\fR
who depends on a file; \-\-transitive is the blast radius
.TP
.B brain twin at \fI<prefix> <ms|30m|2h|1d|git\-hash>\fR
the twin as it was: bi\-temporal read at a moment or commit
.TP
.B brain twin search \fI<substring>\fR
find twinned entities by name
.TP
.B brain twin insights \fI<prefix>\fR
the synthesized picture: churn, hubs, tests, decisions, growth, last sleep
.TP
.B brain twin tests \fI<prefix>\fR
test files, frameworks, covers\-relations, failing cases
.TP
.B brain twin stale \fI<prefix>\fR
docs invalidated by later changes to files they mention
.TP
.B brain ingest \fI<dir> [\-\-prefix <p>]\fR
alias for twin refresh
.TP
.B brain note \fI<name> <text...>\fR
attach a durable note to any entity
.TP
.B brain notes \fI<name>\fR
read an entity's notes, in true order
.TP
.B brain observations \fI<name>\fR
an entity's full observation timeline
.TP
.B brain twin config \fI<prefix> [\-\-add\-extensions csv]\fR
teach extra file extensions to ingest (additive, size\-capped); no flag shows current
.TP
.B brain relation retract \fI<from> <predicate> <to> [\-\-prefix <p>]\fR
mark an edge as no longer holding; history stays, readers stop seeing it
.TP
.B brain relation list \fI<name> [\-\-all] [\-\-prefix <p>]\fR
an entity's live relations, both directions; \-\-all includes retracted
.SH DOCUMENTS
The why and the contract: decisions (ADRs), plans, skills, agent configuration, templates with conformance, and artifacts of graph\-taught kinds.
.TP
.B brain adr add \fI<md\-file> \-\-prefix <p> [\-\-title T] [\-\-status S]\fR
record a decision from any markdown file
.TP
.B brain adr list|show \fI<prefix> [slug]\fR
decisions with status; show prints text, status timeline, mentions
.TP
.B brain plan add|list|show \fI...\fR
the same for plans (e.g. Claude Code plan files); list hides non\-active without \-\-all
.TP
.B brain plan done|abandon|reopen \fI<prefix> <slug> [\-\-why R]\fR
conclude or revive a plan; finished plans stop rotting and leave the lists
.TP
.B brain artifact set\-lifecycle \fI<prefix> <kind> <slug> <state> [\-\-why R]\fR
explicitly set any artifact's lifecycle (active|done|abandoned|retired|superseded)
.TP
.B brain adr ack \fI<prefix> <slug> [\-\-note T]\fR
reviewed against current code, still accurate \(em resets the staleness clock, file untouched
.TP
.B brain plan ack \fI<prefix> <slug> [\-\-note T]\fR
the same acknowledgement for plans
.TP
.B brain artifact ack \fI<prefix> <kind> <slug> [\-\-note T]\fR
the same acknowledgement for any artifact kind
.TP
.B brain skill add|list|show \fI...\fR
agent skills (SKILL.md), auto\-captured or added explicitly
.TP
.B brain agentcfg add|list|show \fI...\fR
agent configuration: CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, .cursorrules, settings, MCP
.TP
.B brain template seed|list|show \fI[slug]\fR
the deliverable contract as graph data
.TP
.B brain template set \fI<slug> \-\-applies\-to k \-\-capture <globs> [\-\-fields spec] [\-\-requires a,b] [\-\-rot none|info|warn] [\-\-placement P] [\-\-enforce E] [\-\-home g] [\-\-project\-to p] [\-\-extensions e]\fR
teach the store a new artifact kind \(em capture, placement, enforcement, and rot policy as data, no code
.TP
.B brain template fitness \fI[slug] [\-\-prefix <p>]\fR
how each contract version performs: first\-capture conformance, missed fields, artifact outcomes \(em the learning loop's read side
.TP
.B brain template evolve \fI<slug> [\-\-prefix <p>] [\-\-apply]\fR
propose the next contract version from fitness evidence; \-\-apply accepts it (never automatic)
.TP
.B brain artifact new|edit \fI<prefix> <kind> <slug> [\-\-title T] [\-\-file f|\-]\fR
graph\-first authoring: validated at write time (enforced kinds refuse with exit 3), graph_first kinds render a read\-only projection
.TP
.B brain artifact render \fI[dir] [\-\-prefix <p>] [\-\-kind k] [\-\-check]\fR
(re)render projections under docs/brain/; \-\-check reports drift, exit 3 on hand\-edits
.TP
.B brain artifact list|show \fI<prefix> <kind> [slug]\fR
browse artifacts of any kind, built\-in or taught
.TP
.B brain asset add \fI<file> \-\-prefix <p> \-\-for <kind>/<slug> [\-\-depicts <t>]... [\-\-subtype s]\fR
type a binary artifact: owner + declared depicts links give screenshots a staleness story
.TP
.B brain asset list \fI<prefix> [\-\-all]\fR
assets with subtype, path, owner, lifecycle
.TP
.B brain deliverable new \fI<template> [\-\-title T]\fR
instantiate a scaffold from the graph to stdout
.SH TESTS
Tests as graph citizens: framework classification and covers\-relations at refresh; imported run protocols with per\-case result timelines.
.TP
.B brain testrun import \fI<report|\-> \-\-prefix <p> [\-\-dir <d>]\fR
ingest cargo\-test output, JUnit XML, or Playwright JSON as a content\-addressed protocol; Playwright's screenshots, videos and traces become assets owned by the case that produced them
.TP
.B brain testrun list \fI<prefix>\fR
imported protocols, newest first
.SH SESSIONS
Who worked here: the coding\-agent sessions that ran in this workspace, with their objective, model, tools and blast radius \(em the graph's only record of a principal.
.TP
.B brain sessions import \fI[dir] [\-\-prefix p] [\-\-agent claude|codex] [\-\-since 2h]\fR
record the coding\-agent sessions that ran in this workspace: objective, model, turns, tools, and the files they edited (never the conversation)
.TP
.B brain sessions list \fI<prefix>\fR
who worked here and what they were trying to do, most recent first
.SH FEATURES
The registry: features as entities, the definition of done as relation predicates, done\-ness as a query.
.TP
.B brain feature add \fI<prefix> <slug> [\-\-title T] [\-\-status S] [\-\-part\-of <parent>]\fR
register (or update) a feature; \-\-part\-of makes it a part of another feature in one act
.TP
.B brain feature link \fI<prefix> <slug> <predicate> <target> [\-\-kind k]\fR
link a feature to files, tests, decisions, docs; part_of joins it to a parent feature
.TP
.B brain feature tree \fI<prefix> [slug]\fR
features and their parts, with readiness rolled up from the leaves
.TP
.B brain feature list|matrix \fI<prefix>\fR
the registry; matrix renders the definition of done as a query
.TP
.B brain done \fI<prefix> <slug>\fR
evaluate a feature against the DoD and record the outcome
.SH BRAIN FUNCTIONS
The functional organs: attention (what matters now), consolidation (distill history into memory), association (what is related, and why).
.TP
.B brain wake \fI<prefix> [\-\-full]\fR
orientation: last sleep, the delta since, attention, warn\-stale, in\-flight work, coherence \(em one command
.TP
.B brain tidy \fI[dir] [\-\-prefix <p>] [\-\-fix \-\-cap fs] [\-\-rm <path>]\fR
clean up: drifted/orphaned projections, retired artifacts, legacy assets, concluded prototypes \(em fixes are governed changes (auditable, revertible); deletion only via explicit \-\-rm
.TP
.B brain attend \fI<prefix> [\-\-top N]\fR
attention: what deserves attention now, ranked with reasons
.TP
.B brain spine \fI<prefix> [\-\-unclaimed <kind>]\fR
what each feature reaches through the files it declares, what no feature claims, and which declared slots nothing corroborates
.TP
.B brain sleep \fI<prefix>\fR
consolidation: distill activity since last sleep into durable memory
.TP
.B brain related \fI<name> [\-\-top N]\fR
association: what is related (co\-change, co\-mention, shared imports)
.TP
.B brain eyes \fI[\-\-prefix P] [\-\-bind IP] [\-\-port N] [\-\-root DIR]\fR
the visual layer for people: judgments as sentences, content you can read, a map of the system \(em read\-only, on localhost
.SH GOVERNED CHANGES
The motor system: mutations to twinned software through the durable intent/receipt boundary, with explicit capability and full provenance.
.TP
.B brain change propose \fI<prefix> <path> \-\-from <file> [\-\-reason R]\fR
propose a change: pure graph write, disk untouched
.TP
.B brain change apply|revert \fI<prefix> <slug> \-\-cap fs\fR
through intent \-> write \-> receipt; refused without the capability
.TP
.B brain change verify \fI<prefix> <slug>\fR
run the repo's test command, link the protocol, grade the change
.TP
.B brain change list|show \fI<prefix> [slug]\fR
the change ledger with status timelines
.TP
.B brain recover
mark pending intents indeterminate and reconcile changes \(em never retries
.SH AUTOMATION
Git triggers the brain: fail\-open hooks on commit and push, an in\-binary watch loop, and regenerated documentation projections.
.TP
.B brain hook install \fI[dir] [\-\-prefix p] [\-\-docs] [\-\-tests] [\-\-test\-cmd c] [\-\-gate]\fR
every git commit/push/checkout/merge triggers the brain; \-\-tests runs the suite, \-\-gate adds the opt\-in pre\-commit refusal (exit 3 blocks; errors fail open)
.TP
.B brain hook status|uninstall \fI[dir]\fR
inspect or remove the hooks (foreign hooks respected)
.TP
.B brain watch \fI[dir] [\-\-prefix p] [\-\-interval s] [\-\-docs]\fR
continuous refresh + insights loop, built into the binary
.TP
.B brain instructions generate \fI[dir] [\-\-prefix p] [\-\-check]\fR
render one guardrail block from the kind registry into CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md \(em every agent family reads identical rules
.TP
.B brain docs generate \fI[dir] [\-\-prefix p] [\-\-out d]\fR
regenerate docs/generated/: tour, screenshots, narrated screencast, man page
.SH NATIVE CODE
The substrate's own calculus: content\-addressed programs, capability\-gated effects, evidence\-cached task checking.
.TP
.B brain put\-code \fI<name> <term>\fR
store a term (.json or .term notation) and bind it
.TP
.B brain notation \fI<file>\fR
convert a term between compact notation and JSON
.TP
.B brain run \fI<name> [\-\-cap <c>]...\fR
evaluate bound code; effects require capabilities
.TP
.B brain task check \fI<task.json> <term>\fR
check a solution, record evidence (cached across alpha\-equivalents)
.TP
.B brain demo
the end\-to\-end demonstration
.SH UTILITIES
Replication, graph inspection, recovery, and the manual itself.
.TP
.B brain refs \fI<name|b3:hash>\fR
reverse edges: who references this node
.TP
.B brain deps \fI<name|b3:hash>\fR
forward edges: what this node references
.TP
.B brain evidence \fI<name|b3:hash>\fR
verification claims about a node
.TP
.B brain bench index \fI[\-\-prefix <p>]\fR
cortex vs cold replay \(em answers verified identical before timing
.TP
.B brain man \fI[\-\-install] [\-\-out <file>]\fR
this manual (troff); \-\-install writes to ~/.local/share/man
.TP
.B brain version
print the version
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BRAIN_STORE
store directory (default ./.brain)
.TP
.B BRAIN_INDEX
set to 'mem' to force a cold reference\-backend rebuild instead of the cortex checkpoint
.TP
.B BRAIN_TTS_MODEL
TTS model for docs narration (default Qwen/Qwen3\-TTS\-12Hz\-0.6B\-Base; espeak\-ng is the fallback)
.SH FILES
.TP
.B .brain/objects/
immutable content\-addressed objects (canonical JSON; identity = BLAKE3 of bytes)
.TP
.B .brain/events.jsonl
append\-only event log \(em the WAL every derived index replays
.TP
.B .brain/intents.jsonl
durable intent/receipt state for the effect boundary
.TP
.B .brain/HEAD
NodeId of the current namespace object
.TP
.B .brain/cortex.json
the cortex checkpoint \(em derived, disposable, rebuilt if missing
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Brownfield minute\-one
.nf
brain init
brain twin backfill . \-\-prefix twin/app
brain twin refresh  . \-\-prefix twin/app
brain hook install \-\-tests
brain attend twin/app
.fi
.SS The session rhythm
.nf
brain attend twin/app          # wake: what matters now
...work; commits refresh the twin and run the suite...
brain twin stale twin/app      # fix rotted docs
brain sleep twin/app           # consolidate before you go
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on error, 2 on usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
docs/twin.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/calculus.md, and the ADRs under docs/adr/ \- all captured in the graph itself (\fBbrain adr list twin/self\fR).
